  "live_records": {
    "q-75255": {
      "dom_id": "step-q75255",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=13-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{0,1,2\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14270560/assets/4faf932e63a57d2fe53fb3942cfe21c65d0d2a88692c665b2706bd68164855c9.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=13-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=13-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14270560/assets/e70e2cf07b27a91c34e59435229302f3b2127b15a2f39049c0a8389cd6f59863.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14270560/assets/aa3858dba149ebf5650ed06f75444244494fe0a961f897100914d54f6d7c0b49.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,2)=8 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,2)=5 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(1,3)=3 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(2,3)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=8+5+3+0=16.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
