    "q-122809": {
      "dom_id": "step-q122809",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14270560/assets/5d5af7cb2f2b12a52bb624d12938aafd2d34b079ad5d28dc44133292b98956ec.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*",
      "worked_solution": "To calculate the lower Riemann sum $L$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $3$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nL={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31}).\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=\\text{Area}({R}_{31})=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =2\\cdot {m}_{11}+2\\cdot {m}_{21}+2\\cdot {m}_{31} \\\\  & =2({m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{31}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-122809-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{m}_{11}-{m}_{21}-{m}_{31}",
              "html": " <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"40\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msub><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45A TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msub><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-msub space=\"3\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45A TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msub><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-msub space=\"3\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45A TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msub></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>21</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>31</mn></mrow></msub></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-122809-b",
